X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Triangleland": "https://triangleland.org/event/big-woods-hike"}
X-SOURCE-ID:triangleland
X-SOURCE:Triangle Land Conservancy
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261101T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261101T113000
DTSTAMP:20261014T201547Z
CREATED:20261014T171520Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T201547Z
UID:10000123-1793523600-1793532600@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Big Woods Hike
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC to explore a special Chatham County preserve!\nThis will be the first public hike at Big Woods Nature Preserve\, the second-largest single purchase by TLC in Chatham county. This preserve\, which is not open to the public\, is also TLC's first acquisition of land directly bordering Jordan Lake's protected land in a decade. \n\nNick Adams\, TLC's Senior Land Manager West\, and TLC Trail Guide\, Steve Gartrell\, will talk about the ecology of Big Woods and TLC's journey to acquiring the property. Due to the lack of developed trails\, this hike requires traversing on uneven ground\, steep inclines\, and over a small stream crossing. Big Woods has a fairly open understory and rugged topography that hosts mature oak-hickory forests\, mixed mesic forests\, and a rich floodplain along Bush Creek. This hike will be approximately 2 miles\, with about 260 feet of elevation gain. This is a free event\, but preregistration is required. Since this is a private property\, the exact location will be sent via email after registration.\n\n 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/big-woods-hike
LOCATION:Big Woods Private Preserve\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
