DTSTAMP:20261031T052604Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54152796248518
DTSTART:20261101T203000Z
DTEND:20261101T223000Z
DESCRIPTION:*Registration required to reserve your spot* Follow the link ab
 ove to reserve your spot.        The registration link will be available s
 tarting 10/18/26.\n\nJoin a Lake James State Park Ranger for a boat tour o
 n beautiful Lake James! Participants will enjoy approximately two hours on
  the water while exploring key landmarks around the park\, and learning ab
 out its fascinating history and natural resources. As we cruise along the 
 shoreline\, we will keep our eyes open for wildlife\, waterfowl\, and Bald
  Eagles. This will be an opportunity to experience Lake James State Park f
 rom a different perspective with a focus on the Catawba River and Paddy's 
 Creek areas of the lake. \n\nMeeting Location: Lake James State Park Cataw
 ba River Access-In the Breezeway\nDuration: Approximately 2 hours 3:30PM-5
 :30PM\n\nPlease Bring: Personal floatation device(we can provide basic PFD
 s if needed)\, water\, sunglasses\, and a jacket. \n\nThings to know: Part
 icipants may bring cameras or other items they feel will make them comfort
 able but please pack light as space will be limited on the boat. Everybody
  must register prior to the event to have a spot on the boat. Registration
  is only for the name listed\, children or spouses have to register separa
 tely. Space is limited to 6 people. If you cannot make it please call us s
 o we can open the spot for another person.
GEO:35.732454;-81.904016
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Catawba River Access\, Breezeway at restro
 oms
SUMMARY:An Evening on the Lake
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/an-evening-on-the-lake
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Youth & Family Activities
END:VEVENT
