X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/foa-annual-meeting-remembering-the-american-revolution-in-the-cherokee-homeland"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261031T052604Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54372080793095
DTSTART:20261104T190000Z
DTEND:20261104T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:FOA Annual Meeting & Program presentation this year is Remember
 ing the American Revolution in the Cherokee Homeland.\n\nCommemorating the
  American Revolution poses particular challenges if one lives in far Weste
 rn North Carolina. Here in the Cherokee ancestral homelands\, the Revoluti
 on brought a bitter and destructive conflict over Cherokee land\, with a p
 ortion of the Cherokee population entering the war as members of a British
 -allied coalition of Indigenous peoples. That war\, in turn\, belonged to 
 a much longer struggle to protect Cherokee land and the wellbeing of Chero
 kee communities – a struggle that preceded the Revolution and continued 
 long after 1776. In this presentation\, Shana Bushyhead Condill (Eastern B
 and of Cherokee Indians)\, Executive Director of the Museum of the Cheroke
 e People\, and Andrew Denson\, professor of history at Western Carolina Un
 iversity\, will discuss the challenges involved in remembering the Revolut
 ion in the mountain region. In particular\, they will examine the planning
  and creation of the Museum of the Cherokee People’s current exhibition\
 , Unrelenting: Cherokee People and the American Revolution. Register for t
 he program before November 04.\n\nA brief presentation of Friends of the A
 rchives business will follow the program at approximately 3 p.m.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:FOA Annual Meeting: Remembering the American Revolution in the Cher
 okee Homeland
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/foa-annual-meeting-rememberi
 ng-the-american-revolution-in-the-cherokee-homeland
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/remembering-the-american-revolution-in-the-cherokee-homeland"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261031T052604Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53974826105482
DTSTART:20261104T190000Z
DTEND:20261104T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:Shana Bushyhead Condill (Eastern Band of Cherokee Indians)\, Ex
 ecutive Director of the Museum of the Cherokee People\, and Andrew Denson\
 , professor of history at Western Carolina University\, will discuss the c
 hallenges involved in remembering the Revolution in the mountain region. I
 n particular\, they will examine the planning and creation of the Museum o
 f the Cherokee People’s current exhibition\, Unrelenting: Cherokee Peopl
 e and the American Revolution. The Friends of the Archives annual business
  meeting will follow the program at approximately 3 p.m.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Remembering the American Revolution in the Cherokee Homeland
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/remembering-the-american-rev
 olution-in-the-cherokee-homeland
