DESCRIPTION:Interested in careers involving people\, technology\, research 
 and meaningful public impact?\n\n \n\nJoin the UNC School of Data and Info
 rmation Sciences on Wednesday\, Nov. 4\, from 5–6 p.m. in Manning Hall\,
  Room 307\, to meet current students and faculty in UNC’s Master of Scie
 nce in Information Science (MSIS) and Master of Science in Library Science
  (MSLS) programs. Explore information careers and discover how an MSIS or 
 MSLS degree can connect your undergraduate interests to your future.\n\n \
 n\nOur graduates pursue a wide range of careers\, including data analyst\,
  user experience designer\, archivist and academic\, public and school lib
 rarian.\n\n \n\nReady to take the next step? Learn how\, as a UNC undergra
 duate\, you could earn your master’s degree in as few as three semesters
 . Snacks will be provided!
