X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/a-conversation-with-holden-thorp-documenting-facts-during-turmoil"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261031T051649Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54310336076501
DTSTART:20261104T230000Z
DTEND:20261105T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join UNC Hussman's Center for Innovation and Sustainability in 
 Local Media for a Media 2030 conversation with Holden Thorp\, editor-in-ch
 ief of the “Science” family of journals. The discussion will explore h
 ow we know what’s true\, how facts are documented and verified\, and how
  AI and political pressures affect the institutions that shape public know
 ledge.\n \n\nAbout Holden Thorp\n\nHolden Thorp is editor-in-chief of the 
 “Science“ family of journals\, a position he has held since 2019. He p
 reviously served as provost of Washington University in St. Louis from 201
 3 to 2019 and as UNC-Chapel Hill’s 10th chancellor from 2008 to 2013.\n\
 n \n\nThorp writes about science\, artificial intelligence\, scientific pu
 blishing and the institutions that shape research and public understanding
 . His recent work has examined AI’s effects on scientific research and p
 ublishing\, debates over social media and teen mental health and the press
 ures facing universities.\n\n \n\nRegistration\n\nThis event is free and o
 pen to the public. Please RSVP on Eventbrite. Carolina students can regist
 er on Heel Life for CLE credit.
GEO:35.910043;-79.05257
LOCATION:Chapman Hall\, 0211
SUMMARY:A Conversation with Holden Thorp: Documenting Facts During Turmoil
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/a-conversation-with-holden-tho
 rp-documenting-facts-during-turmoil
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
