DESCRIPTION:Help us decorate Washington’s Victory Tree!\n\nJoin the Daugh
 ters of the American Revolution (DAR)\, Virginia Dare Chapter for a free o
 rnament crafting workshop in preparation for the Liberty & Light: Washingt
 on’s Victory Tree Celebration that will take place on December 7 in the 
 Dare County Administration Building lobby. Celebrate our nation's history 
 and help bring Washington’s Victory Tree to life—one ornament at a tim
 e!\n\nAll supplies will be provided by the DAR Virginia Dare Chapter. No c
 rafting experience is necessary!\n\nCall to reserve your spot. \n\nWorksho
 p dates:\n\nBaum Senior Center in Kill Devil Hills Tuesday\, November 3\, 
 2026 | 10 a.m.–12 p.m. Call 252.475.5635 to reserve your spot.Fessenden 
 Community Center in Buxton Thursday\, November 5\, 2026 | 10 a.m.–12 p.m
 . Call 252.475.5653 to reserve your spot.Virginia Tillett Community Center
  in Manteo Friday\, November 6\, 2026 | 10 a.m.–12 p.m. Call 252.475.927
 0 to reserve your spot. \n\nWashington’s Victory Tree will be on display
  for the holiday season inside the Dare County Administration lobby\, begi
 nning on December 7. Participants will create ornaments for the Victory Tr
 ee\, including lanterns\, tricorn hats and cloth stars. Participants will 
 also make one small ornament to take home
GEO:35.268884;-75.539414
LOCATION:Dare A250
SUMMARY:Liberty & Light: Community Ornament Crafting Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/liberty-light-community-orna
 ment-crafting-workshop
END:VEVENT
