BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Naturalsciences": "https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/museum-movie-night-jurassic-park/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:naturalsciences
X-SOURCE:NC Museum of Natural Sciences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T220000
DTSTAMP:20261031T012628
CREATED:20251106T182738Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261028T180036Z
UID:114900-1793986200-1794002400@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Museum Movie Night: Jurassic Park
DESCRIPTION:Jurassic Park (1993)\n“Yeah\, but\, John\, if The Pirates of the Caribbean breaks down\, the pirates don’t eat the tourists.” \nHold onto your butts; science just brought dinosaurs back to life! Step into a theme park where cloning meets chaos\, and T. rex steals the show. It’s a thrilling mix of cutting-edge science\, prehistoric power\, and popcorn-worthy adventure that reminds us: just because we can\, doesn’t mean we should. \nThis movie is rated PG-13. \nMuseum Movie Night — a night of movies\, music\, and mind-blowing fun. Before the show\, enjoy live tunes\, hands-on science activities\, and tasty food and drinks. After the credits roll\, stick around for a science chat with an expert and movie trivia\, all hosted by A/V Geeks! \n  \nCheck out the upcoming movies and learn more about Museum Movie Night: Where Science meets the Cinema. \nBuy Tickets \n\nSchedule\n5:30pm–7pm: Live music and science stations. Food and drinks for sale.\n7pm: Movie begins in the WRAL 3D Theater\, followed by commentary and movie trivia. \nStay after the movie for trivia and Q&A with our expert\, Dr. Jennifer Anné\, Assistant Manager of the SECU DinoLab \n \n\nExhibits and Activities\nSimply saying that proteins\, uh… preserve \nMeet the paleoproteomics team from NCSU\, the real miracle workers when it comes to ancient molecule preservation. Learn what is possible\, and what is not\, in the world of dino molecules. In addition to the modern molecular world\, learn how the science fiction of Jurassic Park inspired scientist to start digging into the realm of ancient molecular studies with our local science historian\, Dr. Elizabeth Jones. \nDino Dig \nSee what mini treasures you can excavate! \nPaper Circuits \nLearn how circuits work and create a light-up card to take home! \nDino DNA Craft \nChoose a dino\, shrink it\, and pop it in a test tube! You never know when you’ll need some dino DNA! \nThey Could Be Dinos \nWell…maybe not\, but these live animals have some prehistoric vibes!
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/museum-movie-night-jurassic-park/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,All Ages,Children,General Events,Museum Movie Night,Special Events,Teens,WRAL 3D Theater
ORGANIZER;CN="Miranda%20Dowdy":MAILTO:miranda.dowdy@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822735;-78.6395502
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Downtown Raleigh 11 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=11 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6395502,35.7822735
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/getting-proper-about-prompting-an-introduction-to-prompt-engineering-for-social-science-and-survey-research-6958"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261031T051650Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52259497407699
DTSTART:20261106T180000Z
DTEND:20261106T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Take a glance through recent news or social media and you would
  be hard-pressed not to see mentions of chatbots and artificial intelligen
 ce (AI) methods aimed at generating text\, images and other content.  Rece
 nt work by Eloundou and colleagues (2023) explored the potential impact of
  these types of generative AI on labor markets\, and survey research\, spe
 cifically was among the top two most impacted industries.  Professor Andre
 w Ng has been cited as saying “AI won’t replace human workers\, but 
 ‘people that use it will replace people that don’t.’”  Much of the
  way researchers in the social sciences and survey research are incorporat
 ing AI into their workflow involves some type of prompting.  Prompt Engine
 ering approaches along with more nuanced fine tuning approaches are being 
 used and refined to better incorporate more robust approaches for AI incor
 poration into the research process.  In this short course we will provide 
 an overview of the emerging field of prompt engineering and illustrate how
  a prompt engineering approach and problem specification mindset can be us
 eful for maximizing the utility of large language models\, specifically\, 
 within social science.  Concepts and experimental approaches will be illus
 trated using several real-world\, grounded and published work.  The shortc
 ourse also incorporates an experiential component that encourages particip
 ants to apply basic concepts that we cover in the course in real-time as w
 e work on exercises together in the later part of the course.\n\nRegistrat
 ion and fee (refundable for UNCCH students) are required for Zoom link acc
 ess.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Getting Proper about Prompting:  An Introduction to Prompt Engineer
 ing for Social Science and Survey Research
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/getting-proper-about-prompting
 -an-introduction-to-prompt-engineering-for-social-science-and-survey-resea
 rch-6958
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
