CREATED:20261006T002330Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003418Z
UID:10000877-1794056400-1794065400@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Goodbye to Fall Forest Bathing Walk
DESCRIPTION:with Aimee Vandemark\, Certified Forest and Nature Therapy Guide \nForest Therapy (sometimes known as Forest Bathing or Shinrin-Yoku) broadly means taking in the forest atmosphere with all of one’s senses. Not simply a walk in the woods; it is the conscious and contemplative practice of being immersed in the sights\, sounds\, and smells of the forest. During your walk\, Aimee Vandemark will guide you through invitations to awaken your senses\, slow down\, be present\, and reconnect with the nature and rhythm of your surroundings. Minimum Age: 18 \nREGISTER HERE \nRegistration is managed by the program leader. \nRegistration deadline: Friday\, November 6 at 10 a.m.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/goodbye-to-fall-forest-bathing-walk-2/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Health and Wellbeing
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=North Carolina Botanical Garden 100 Old Mason Farm Road Chapel Hill NC 27517 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=100 Old Mason Farm Road:geo:-79.031939,35.901081
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncbg": "https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/fall-hike-pennys-bend/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncbg
X-SOURCE:NC Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T160000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003014Z
CREATED:20261006T003014Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003014Z
UID:10000880-1794056400-1794067200@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Fall Hike at Penny's Bend Nature Preserve
DESCRIPTION:Experience the beauty of autumn at Penny’s Bend Nature Preserve\, an 84-acre natural area in northeast Durham managed by the North Carolina Botanical Garden. Surrounded on three sides by the Eno River\, this unique preserve protects mature forests\, open prairies\, and populations of regionally rare plants. Explore the fall landscape while learning about Penny’s Bend’s distinctive natural communities and how the Garden’s stewardship helps conserve this ecologically significant preserve. This program counts toward the field trip requirement for the Certificate in Native Plants program. \nFee: $20 ($18 Members) \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/fall-hike-pennys-bend/
LOCATION:Penny’s Bend Nature Preserve\, Old Oxford Rd\, Durham\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Hikes and Tours,Learn
GEO:36.0860873;-78.8475216
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Penny’s Bend Nature Preserve Old Oxford Rd Durham NC United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=Old Oxford Rd:geo:-78.8475216,36.0860873
END:VEVENT
