DTSTART:20261107T143000Z
DTEND:20261107T213000Z
DESCRIPTION:Discover how primary sources can bring history to life. Join Ca
 rolina K-12 and the State Archives of North Carolina in this FREE hands-on
  workshop! Teachers will explore World War II through letters\, military r
 ecords\, photographs\, and archival materials from North Carolina veterans
 . Participants will hear from author Ann McColl\, work with historians and
  archivists from the State Archives of North Carolina\, develop classroom 
 applications\, and attend a special staged reading of More Than War. Educa
 tors will leave with ready-to-use resources and fresh ideas for teaching h
 istory through authentic documents. Apply here by October 23rd!\n\nDate: S
 aturday\, November 7\, 2026\nLocation: State Archives of North Carolina an
 d Burning Coal Theater\nSchedule: 9:30 AM - 4:30 PM\nCost: Free for select
 ed teachers (lunch provided)\nSpace available: Approximately 20 teachers\n
 CEUs: 7 hours (0.7)\nBecause space is limited\, submitting this form does 
 not guarantee a spot. Carolina K-12 will contact selected participants by 
 email.
LOCATION:State Archives of North Carolina and Burning Coal Theater
SUMMARY:Sold Out: Teacher Workshop: Veterans\, Primary Sources\, and the St
 ories They Tell
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/teacher-workshop-veterans-pr
 imary-sources-and-the-stories-they-tell
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
