DESCRIPTION:Join the American Indian Center and American Studies for our 20
 26 Michael D. Green Lecture. Our guest lecturer this year is Lokosh\, (Jos
 hua D. Hinson)\, a citizen of the Chickasaw Nation. He will a give a lectu
 re titled "Beloved Speech\, Sacred Image: Chikashsha poetry and art in the
  twenty-first century."\n\n \n\nReception begins at 4:00 PM\; Lecture is a
 t 5:00 PM.\n\n \n\nA fluent speaker of the Chickasaw language\, poet\, and
  an award-winning artist\, he holds a PhD in Native Language Revitalizatio
 n from the University of Oklahoma. He writes and makes art on the Chickasa
 w Nation Reservation\, Ada\, Oklahoma.
GEO:35.913407;-79.052875
LOCATION:Hyde Hall\, University Room
SUMMARY:Michael D. Green Lecture in American Indian & Indigenous Studies
