DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261112T160000
DTSTAMP:20260915T130805Z
CREATED:20260706T124032Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T130805Z
UID:17502-1794492000-1794499200@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Botanical Quilt Blocks
DESCRIPTION:Learn to hand-stitch a garden-inspired quilt block in this two-hour class with Julia Gartrell\, artist and creator of the Radical Repair Workshop\, that will prepare you for a cozy winter season.  Using pre-cut fabric\, students can design their own block with the selection of colors provided. Pick from four fun blocks: a tulip\, a primrose\, a ladybug or a mushroom. No sewing experience needed\, but a basic understanding of hand stitching will be helpful.  Supplies will be provided. \nFee: $42; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nLocation: Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center.\n \nAccessibility: This program takes place seated in an indoor location accessible via paved surfaces and equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/botanical-quilt-blocks/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Quilt-Julia-Gartrell-chenilledetail-220x220-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
