X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group African American Cultural Center": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/learning-lab-fashion-lab-and-clothing-swap"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_african_american_cultural_center
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20261031T052628Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53419087955591
DTSTART:20261112T220000Z
DTEND:20261113T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Your style tells a story before you say a word. In this interac
 tive workshop\, we'll explore how fashion can be a powerful form of self-e
 xpression and a reflection of who you are. Whether you're figuring out you
 r signature look\, building a wardrobe on a budget or getting ready for in
 ternships\, interviews and everyday campus life\, you'll discover how to d
 ress in a way that feels authentic\, confident and completely you. You'll 
 leave with practical tips\, fresh inspiration and a new perspective on usi
 ng your personal style to make a lasting impression — without pretending
  to be anyone else.\n\nThis event will include thrifted clothing items and
  a clothing swap.  Light refreshments and snacks will be served.\n\nIf you
  have any questions\, contact Andaiye Qaasim\, assistant director of the A
 frican American Cultural Center\, at aaqaasim@ncsu.edu.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (Sec
 ond-Floor Library and Gallery)
SUMMARY:Learning Lab: Authentically You: Personal Style as a Branding Tool
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/learning-lab-fashion-lab-and-
 clothing-swap
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training
CATEGORIES:Student Life
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-human-and-wellbeing"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261031T051650Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54356196986775
DTSTART:20261112T223000Z
DTEND:20261113T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Is AI a threat to human health and happiness\, or can it be har
 nessed to improve human wellbeing? How can we maximize its benefits while 
 minimizing its risks?\n\nJoin us to hear a range of perspectives on how AI
  may affect human wellbeing. Alessandra Bazzano is a professor who studies
  the relationship between AI and public health. Tyler Cowen is an economis
 t and professor at George Mason University. Ben Levinstein is a philosophe
 r and member of technical staff at Anthropic. The conversation will be mod
 erated by UNC journalism professor Deb Aikat.\n\nThe event is co-sponsored
  by The Office of the Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost. \n\nStudents 
 who attend in person can earn CLE credit. No tickets necessary\; seating i
 s first-come\, first-served. Reserved tickets are available for guests com
 ing from outside Chapel Hill\; email publicdiscourse@unc.edu to reserve se
 ats. Join us for pizza in the lobby afterward!
LOCATION:Frank Porter Graham Student Union Auditorium
SUMMARY:AI Human and Wellbeing
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-human-and-wellbeing
END:VEVENT
