UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54276932019787
DTSTART:20261116T133000Z
DTEND:20261116T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Calling all water-loving educators!!!\n\nJoin the NC Museum of 
 Natural Sciences this November to explore North Carolina’s beautiful Coh
 arie River. We will learn about the Riverkeepers restoration initiatives a
 nd hear directly from members of the Coharie Tribe about their experiences
  living along the river. Become familiar with one of North Carolina’s wi
 ld areas and connect with the long history of the people who call this lan
 d home. \n\nThis is an day-long event on Monday\, November 16th. Cost: $75
  (this includes the kayak rental and lunch). Participants will ride with t
 he group from Raleigh departing at 8:30am. Transportation will be in Museu
 m vans or bus.\n\nRead more and register HERE!\n\nThe full workshop fee is
  due when you register and payment is via credit card. Registration for mo
 st Educator Treks is on a first-come\, first-served basis. Treks fill quic
 kly\, so register early!
LOCATION:Depart from North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY:Educator Trek: Great Coharie River Paddling Tour
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/educator-trek-great-coharie-
 river-paddling-tour
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Outdoor Recreation (kayak\, paddle\, hikes)
CATEGORIES:Nature & Wildlife Programs
END:VEVENT
