DTEND:20261116T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join a park ranger for a scenic boat tour along the beautiful s
 hores of Lake James! Discover the natural beauty of the lake as we explore
  its quiet coves\, wooded shorelines\, and diverse wildlife habitats. Keep
  your eyes open for birds\, wildlife\, and breathtaking landscapes. Whethe
 r you’re an experienced photographer\, a beginner\, or simply someone th
 at wants to use your phone and see wildlife from a different perspective\,
  this is for you.\n\nMeeting Location: Lake James Park Paddy's Creek Acces
 s - East Shelter\n\nDuration: Approximately 2 hours 9:00am - 11am\n\nPleas
 e Bring: Water\, personal floatation device (provided if you do not have) 
 sunglasses.\n\nEverybody must register prior to the event to have a spot o
 n the boat. Registration is only for the name listed\; children or spouses
  must register separately. Space is limited to 6 people. If you cannot mak
 e it\, please call us so we can open the spot for another person
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Paddy's Creek Access
SUMMARY:Snapshots and Shorelines: A guided photograph tour
