UID:5drhdmrgv5f9bqmm9e1kadr8kc@google.com__20261120
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260713T172355Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy. In the summer mon
 ths\, we will meet from on Fridays 8-9am at MLK and Hope Valley Road. Star
 ting in September\, we will shift back to the afternoons from 4-5:00pm at 
 South Roxboro St. &amp\; Martin Luther King Jr. Parkway\, Durham\, NC 2771
 3.\n\nFor the summer months (am time)\, parking is best at St Andrew&#39\;
 s Court or Reynolds Avenue N.\n\nThis will be a POSITIVE and nonviolent de
 monstration. We are here to protect our democracy. We are standing up for 
 what we believe in. We want to inspire people to join us and grow our move
 ment!\n\nPlease bring positive signs only. Some examples: Instead of &quot
 \;Stop defunding science&quot\; Say &quot\;Protect Research&quot\; &quot\;
 Immigrants make us stronger&quot\; &quot\;Housing for all&quot\; &quot\;He
 althcare for all&quot\; &quot\;Save the planet&quot\;\n\nMake signs about 
 what you&#39\;re standing up for -- whether that is the libraries\, DEI\, 
 healthcare\, women’s rights\n\nPlease no mocking signs\, no swastikas\n\
 nWe are excited to see you there and stand together for our country!\n\nSe
 e you every Friday engaging drivers in Durham.\n\nPlease join our Substack
 : <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://substack.com/profile/11548
 4101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd
 =2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3y7Kv9RwiMPWcPPUFQih9k" target="_blank">https://substack
 .com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy</a>\n\nFor more ED4D 
 Mobilize Events: <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.mobiliz
 e.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=
 2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1xqNbFip0P6DfK4plFB1D7" target="_blank">https://www.mobil
 ize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/</a>\n\n<a href="https://www.google.com
 /url?q=https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/event/841321/&a
 mp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw23z_bx1AhXDbf2eL54
 BRH5" target="_blank">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/
 event/841321/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260713T172355Z
LOCATION:Martin Luther King Junior Parkway & Hope Valley Road\, Durham\, N
 C\, 27707
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:ICE Is Not Welcome Here! Cary ICE Detention Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T110000
DTSTAMP:20261031T052534Z
UID:ong6reckd2k3ag9dj2572ku0om@google.com__20261120
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20260212T203737Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy as will gather to 
 demonstrate at the ICE facility in Cary. We will stand along Evans Road at
  the corner of Evans and Centrewest Court\, near the Cary ICE office (140 
 Centrewest Ct\, Cary). \n\nParking is available along Centrewest Court\, o
 r along Quade Drive (off Evans Road). This action serves to let ICE know w
 e do not welcome them here and also make community residents aware that IC
 E has an office - and an ongoing presence - right here in Cary.\n\nThis wi
 ll be a nonviolent demonstration. We are here to say ICE is not welcome. W
 e are standing up for what we believe in. We want to inspire people to joi
 n us and grow our movement!\n\nPlease bring signs\; no swastikas please.\n
 \nWe are excited to see you there and stand together for our country and l
 et ICE know they are not welcome!\n\nSee you every Friday morning engaging
  drivers in Cary.\n\nPlease join our Substack: <a href="https://www.google
 .com/url?q=https://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-demo
 cracy&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3y7Kv9RwiMP
 WcPPUFQih9k" target="_blank">https://substack.com/profile/115484101-engage
 d-defenders-4-democracy</a>\n\nFor more ED4D Mobilize Events: <a href="htt
 ps://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocr
 acy/&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1xqNbFip0P6D
 fK4plFB1D7" target="_blank">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemo
 cracy/</a>\n\n<a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.mobilize.u
 s/engagedefendersfordemocracy/event/896777/&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar
 &amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3T8EtOQ8r0gLPlo0-wcFO3" target="_blank">https:/
 /www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/event/896777/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260306T223234Z
LOCATION:ICE headquarters\, 140 Centrewest Ct\, Cary\, NC\, 27513
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Triangleland": "https://triangleland.org/event/trail-talks-with-tlc-williamson"}
X-SOURCE-ID:triangleland
X-SOURCE:Triangle Land Conservancy
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T113000
DTSTAMP:20261014T195607Z
CREATED:20261014T190058Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T195607Z
UID:10000125-1795167000-1795174200@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Trail Talks with TLC: Williamson
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC staff for guided nature journaling at Williamson Nature Preserve!\nSlow down and connect with nature with Senior Volunteer and Outreach Associate\, Amaya Horner! Amaya will give a brief history of Williamson Nature Preserve and talk about the types of programs that this working farm and public preserve offers. Then\, we will navigate Two Ponds Loop\, making stops along the way to collect observations about the world around us using nature journaling methods curated by naturalist and educator\, John Muir Laws.\n\nPlease bring your own journal and writing utensils\, but we will have some extra materials on hand. Participants will receive a Quick Start Guide to Nature Journaling zine written by John Muir Laws and the Wild Wonder Foundation to take home! This will be a slow\, 1.5 mile hike on uneven terrain. Bring a full water bottle and a mat or blanket to sit on for the still moments on trail.  This event is free\, but preregistration is required.\n\n 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/trail-talks-with-tlc-williamson
LOCATION:Williamson Farm and Nature Preserve\, 4429 Old Country Mial Rd\, Raleigh\, 27610\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Triangleland": "https://triangleland.org/event/nature-storytime-forest-detectives-2"}
X-SOURCE-ID:triangleland
X-SOURCE:Triangle Land Conservancy
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T113000
DTSTAMP:20261027T210421Z
CREATED:20261027T210421Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027T210421Z
UID:10000130-1795168800-1795174200@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Nature Storytime: Forest Detectives
DESCRIPTION:Become a Forest Detective at our monthly Nature Storytime!\nEngage your sense of smell\, sight\, sound\, and wonder! This month’s story time will invite everyone to learn about the cycles and secrets of nature through nature stories\, nature games\, and a short ramble through the Brumley Nature Preserve. Join a TLC educator for this monthly story series where you can meet other families in your community and learn about nature. This month's nature stories are: "All Around Us" By Xelena Gomez and "Beneath" by Cori Doerrfeld. This program is designed for kids age 3-7 and their grownups. Please register all members of the family attending\, including children and adults. This event is free\, but preregistration is required:
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/nature-storytime-forest-detectives-2
LOCATION:Brumley South Nature Preserve\, 3055 New Hope Church Rd\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_f511c08827b961733168ea93761e472cd12de35e813c3a73af3e44c56b7fe53d
SUMMARY:UU Justice NC’s Friday Action Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T120000
DTSTAMP:20261031T052534Z
UID:1tvd180uho6fnokuhaj2c5h1k8_R20251107T160000@google.com__20261120
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20250729T151905Z
DESCRIPTION:11:00am-12:00pm: Unitarian Universalist Justice NC’s Friday 
 Action Hour. <a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/w/87452791684?_x_zm_rtaid=7M
 gmJB_hSsCKh3xUYHZrBA.1750590489156.1865f9b53934845e34cb2d06c2d1adc5&_x_zm_
 rhtaid=5#success" target="_blank"><u>Zoom here </u></a><br><u> </u><br><
 p>Since May of 2020\, North Carolina UUs and friends have gathered on Frid
 ays to take action and experience the joy and power of community. Every Fr
 iday at 11:00am we recap the past week and take action on the issues impac
 ting our state and country. And there is always great music to help us fee
 l the justice movement in our bones! ALL are welcome! We are also blessed 
 to be joined by Unitarian Universalists\, our beloved North Carolina justi
 ce partners\, and dear friends from outside our state (shout out to our We
 st Virginia fam!).</p><p>You can join us <strong>every Friday </strong>at 
 11:00 am via this <a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/tZMpcu
 uvpzosEtAhdqFHrSySSb6REM8wkPru">Zoom link</a>. And if you can't make it on
  Fridays\, you can still take action at any time - just check out our <a h
 ref="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Fwj6m0Qw4fAH_keuIoUNgdSWslBZzVgQ5
 NCgVPm_L-U/edit?tab=t.0" class="pastedDriveLink-0">Weekly action list</a>.
  And sign up for our <a href="https://secure.everyaction.com/QSBiJQ1YQEGwP
 O2KMIRIkQ2" target="_blank">Weekly Friday Action Hour Email</a> that inclu
 des a promo of the week's actions\, Zoom link\, and link to our Actions Go
 ogle Doc.</p><p><a href="https://www.uujusticenc.org/get-involved/friday-a
 ction-hour/">https://www.uujusticenc.org/get-involved/friday-action-hour/<
 /a> </p><u> </u>
