DTSTAMP:20261031T052614Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54321336469894
DTSTART:20261122T150000Z
DTEND:20261122T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:High on the Hog!\n\nHogs were very important to families in the
  backcountry during the late 18th century and butchering occurred in late 
 fall to early winter. Join us for a day of processing various cuts of hog 
 meat into dishes that would have been served to families in the late 18th 
 century.\n\nWe will be making sausage from scratch\, using methods and tec
 hniques from the 18th century. We will prepare pickled pigs’ feet and a 
 pork roast with sauerkraut. Although tasting is prohibited\, the smells ar
 e free!
GEO:35.078;-80.882745
LOCATION:President James K. Polk Historic Site
SUMMARY:Historical Hearth Cooks Demonstration
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/historical-hearth-cooks-demo
 nstration-4020
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
END:VEVENT
