X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20261031T052629Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53550588367830
DTSTART:20270115T150000Z
DTEND:20270115T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center to experience ariana 
 Farquharson's You Are Here: Geolocating the Self through the Familiar in t
 he Midst of the Unfamiliar. The exhibition is a speculative\, immersive wo
 rld-building study that invites guests to explore (geo)locating self and h
 ome amid a rapidly and frequently changing post-pandemic “new” world. 
 It will be on display in the art gallery at the African American Cultural 
 Center from Oct. 28\, 2026\, to  Feb. 28\, 2027. A behind-the-scenes look 
 at the exhibition is set for Nov. 11.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (218
 )
SUMMARY:You Are Here Exhibition
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/you-are-here-geolocating-the-
 self-through-the-familiar-in-the-midst-of-the-unfamiliar-exhibition
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining-north-carolinas-black-heritage"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261031T052617Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138242036828
DTSTART:20270115T150000Z
DTEND:20270115T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/nc-public-librarian-certification-commission-2701"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261031T052617Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53425686332096
DTSTART:20270115T153000Z
DTEND:20270115T173000Z
DESCRIPTION:The NC Public Librarian Certification Commission was formed in 
 1936 to set minimum standards for public librarians to protect and maintai
 n public library resources\, to assure professional management and adminis
 tration of library services\, to meet the personnel requirements for State
  Aid administered by the Library of NC\, and to guarantee the best possibl
 e public library service to all North Carolinians.\n\nThe North Carolina G
 eneral Statute 143B-68 states that the commission must be comprised of: th
 e Chairman of the public libraries section of NCLA\, two individuals named
  by the Governor upon nomination of the NCLA\, the dean of a State or regi
 onally accredited graduate school of librarianship in North Carolina appoi
 nted by the Governor\, and one member at large appointed by the Governor. 
 Commission members appointed by the Governor serve 4-year terms\, all othe
 rs serve 2-year terms.\n\nCommission meetings are held quarterly to review
  applications and discuss Certification policies and procedures.\n\nThe co
 mmission's meeting dates for the 2025-2026 year are October 27\, 2025\, Ja
 nuary 9\, 2026\, April 10\, 2026\, and July 10\, 2026. All meetings are he
 ld at the Library of NC beginning at 1:00 pm unless otherwise posted. Info
 rmation about meetings can be found on the North Carolina Secretary of Sta
 te's meeting calendar.\n\nHave questions about certification? Contact us a
 t NC.Certification.Commission@dncr.nc.gov.
GEO:32.071865;-81.092949
LOCATION:DNCR \, 308
SUMMARY:NC Public Librarian Certification Commission
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/nc-public-librarian-certific
 ation-commission-2701
CATEGORIES:Organizational
CATEGORIES:Public Meetings
END:VEVENT
