BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wake Forest Chamber of Commerce": "https://chambermaster.wakeforestchamber.org/events/details/heritage-business-alliance-in-person-meeting"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wakeforest_chamber
SUMMARY:Heritage Business Alliance In-Person Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270125T050000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270125T060000
UID:1a2bdee2ec607371ae6e15ce9a1cfe4f@growthzone.com
DESCRIPTION:The Heritage Business Alliance (HBA) brings together businesse
 s located in and connected to the Heritage area of Wake Forest to strength
 en relationships\, share information\, and address the unique needs of thi
 s growing business community. HBA members meet quarterly in person to conn
 ect with one another\, discuss issues impacting Heritage businesses\, and 
 identify opportunities for collaboration\, advocacy\, and support. Meeting
 s also provide time to advance the Alliance's plan of work and ensure Heri
 tage businesses have a strong connection to the Wake Forest Area Chamber a
 nd community partners. Heritage-area businesses are encouraged to attend\,
  get involved\, and help shape the work of the Alliance.
LOCATION:Wake Forest\, NC
URL:https://chambermaster.wakeforestchamber.org/events/details/heritage-bu
 siness-alliance-in-person-meeting
X-SOURCE:Wake Forest Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group African American Cultural Center": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/you-are-here-geolocating-the-self-through-the-familiar-in-the-midst-of-the-unfamiliar-exhibition"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_african_american_cultural_center
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20261031T052629Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53550588372956
DTSTART:20270125T150000Z
DTEND:20270125T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center to experience ariana 
 Farquharson's You Are Here: Geolocating the Self through the Familiar in t
 he Midst of the Unfamiliar. The exhibition is a speculative\, immersive wo
 rld-building study that invites guests to explore (geo)locating self and h
 ome amid a rapidly and frequently changing post-pandemic “new” world. 
 It will be on display in the art gallery at the African American Cultural 
 Center from Oct. 28\, 2026\, to  Feb. 28\, 2027. A behind-the-scenes look 
 at the exhibition is set for Nov. 11.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (218
 )
SUMMARY:You Are Here Exhibition
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/you-are-here-geolocating-the-
 self-through-the-familiar-in-the-midst-of-the-unfamiliar-exhibition
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
