BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining-north-carolinas-black-heritage"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261031T052618Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138242045032
DTSTART:20270202T150000Z
DTEND:20270202T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/cognitive-interviewing-in-survey-research-6320"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261031T051651Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53939360242489
DTSTART:20270202T170000Z
DTEND:20270202T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Cognitive interviewing in survey research is a tool that allows
  researchers to improve survey questions and questionnaires by better unde
 rstanding how respondents understand and respond to the questions they are
  being asked. Data gathered through cognitive interviews help researchers 
 identify and remedy issues with their questionnaires. This short course pr
 ovides participants with fundamentals on where cognitive interviews fit in
  the survey process and on how to design\, conduct\, and analyze cognitive
  interviews. Participants will have the opportunity to practice specific c
 ognitive interviewing techniques\, including think-alouds\, probing\, and 
 observation. Participants will also learn about revising survey questions 
 based on interpreting cognitive interview results and about the research o
 n which cognitive interview practices are based.\n\nCourse Goals:\nBy the 
 end of the course\, participants will be able to:\n1. Understand what cogn
 itive interviews are and their use in survey research\n2. Be able to prepa
 re for and conduct cognitive interviews\n3. Improve survey questionnaires 
 and survey items based on cognitive interview data\n\n \n\nRegistration an
 d fee (refundable for Carolina students) are required for Zoom link access
 .\n\nThis event is sponsored by the UNC Odum Institute.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Cognitive Interviewing in Survey Research
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/cognitive-interviewing-in-surv
 ey-research-6320
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
