BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group Gregg Museum Of Art Design": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/the-gregg-museum-edition-ai-hot-topics-does-ai-have-a-place-in-the-aarts"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_gregg_museum_of_art_design
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20261031T052630Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54381416854066
DTSTART:20270303T190000Z
DTEND:20270303T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join the Data Science and AI Academy at the Gregg Museum
  of Art and Design for an exclusive AI Hot Topics event. The Gregg aims to
  create and hold space for the many perspectives surrounding artificial in
 telligence's growing presence in universities\, the arts and even in our e
 veryday lives. This hour-long conversation invites us to do more than take
  a side\; it asks us to listen first\, question and then challenge ourselv
 es to better understand where others are coming from. \n\nAs AI becomes in
 creasingly present in creative spaces\, questions about ethics\, authorshi
 p and what may be at stake for artistic expression continue to emerge. Joi
 n us for an open conversation exploring AI's place in the arts and the pos
 sibilities and concerns that have come with it.\n\nArtists\, students\, fa
 culty and community members will unpack and share various presepctives of 
 who gets to define art and the very real ethical concerns surrounding AI
 ’s impact\, particularly in the arts and education.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Gregg Museum Edition: AI Hot Topics: Does AI Have a Place in the A(
 a)rts?
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/the-gregg-museum-edition-ai-h
 ot-topics-does-ai-have-a-place-in-the-aarts
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group African American Cultural Center": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/learning-lab-fashion-sustainability-and-makerspace"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_african_american_cultural_center
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20261031T052629Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53419106064992
DTSTART:20270303T223000Z
DTEND:20270304T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Don’t throw it away\, rework it.\n\nJoin the African American
  Cultural Center at the D.H. Hill Jr. Library Makerspace for a hands-on di
 ve into sustainable fashion and do-it-yourself creation. Whether you want 
 to learn the basics of how to use a sewing machine\, mend your favorite da
 maged thrifted piece or embroider custom patches to personalize your jacke
 t or tote\, this lab is for you. We’ll cover essential mending technique
 s and show you how to extend the life of your wardrobe through conscious c
 reation. Sewing experience is not necessary to participate.\n\nWe'll provi
 de all machines and materials needed for the session. Bring a piece of clo
 thing you’d like to mend or customize or use the practice fabric provide
 d\n\nIf you have questions about the session\, contact Andaiye Qaasim\, as
 sistant director of the African American Cultural Center\, at aaqaasim@ncs
 u.edu.
GEO:35.787562;-78.669711
LOCATION:D.H. Hill Jr. Library\, Makerspace
SUMMARY:Learning Lab: Fashion Sustainability and Makerspace
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/learning-lab-fashion-sustaina
 bility-and-makerspace
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Student Life
END:VEVENT
